PARSFILE Generic\Links\GenLink_f197e7b1-4953-4b69-b758-1950f96574d0.par
#BlueLink8 Generic Group of Links`Two Blind-Spot Sensors` ADAS Combinations` , Link 9`GenLink_f197e7b1-4953-4b69-b758-1950f96574d0



#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This dataset assembles some traffic vehicles with an ACC Sensor and two blind-spot sensors. The equations used to show the ACC icon and modify the target speed used internally by the CarSim speed controller involve the detection of the closest vehicle.
#
#The equation that modifies the internal target speed uses detection variables such as SpdS<<s>>_1 and MagS<<s>>_1, where <<s>> is the number of the ACC Sensor. These detection variables are created when there is at least one sensor and at least one moving object.
#
#The linked datasets are made to ensure that moving objects (the traffic vehicles) and the ACC Sensor are defined before the link to the ACC Equations.
#
#The moving objects from link 1 follow a target speed defined in link 3. The vehicles from link 3 use a speed assigned to a custom parameter VX_REF.
#
#The lateral positions of the moving objects are set using the LTARG function, with datasets specified with ILTARG.
#
#N_LTARG is the number of LTARG datasets that will be shown in the Echo file. The
#default value is 1; it can be set to any positive number up to 100. In this example it is being used to increment the number of target paths being used and shown in the echo files.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: Generic Data Group; { Traffic and Blind-Spot Sensors } ACC, Blind-Spot, 2 Lanes Fwd, 1 Lane Opp.
